{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in one deterministic specification. The specification keeps all uncontrollable events defined at every state, uses random_walk in the initial clear exploration state, routes obstacle events into dedicated turn-recovery states, avoids forward/random actions in obstacle-reached states, and returns quickly to exploration when path_clear is observed. Action states are one-shot and non-critical path_clear self-loops in commit states so intended pulses are not preempted.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate unconstrained sensing and motion capability in plant automata, with policy enforced by specification automata",
    "Use clear exploration, short forward progress, and dedicated left/right/front recovery states with exactly one controllable action each"
  ],
